  "emailBody": "\n        <html>\n\n        <body\n            style=\"\n                font-family:Segoe UI, Arial, sans-serif;\n                margin:20px;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    background:#d42e12;\n                    color:white;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                \"\n            >\n\n\n               <h1 style=\"margin:0;\">\n                    Fuel Market Intelligence Morning Report\n                </h1>\n\n                <p style=\"margin:5px 0 0 0;\">\n                    11 August 2026\n                </p>\n\n            </div>\n\n            <p\n                style=\"\n                    font-size:16px;\n                    margin-top:20px;\n                    margin-bottom:20px;\n                \"\n            >\n                Good morning Sir,\n                <br><br>\n                \n                Here is today's fuel market intelligence report highlighting\n                the latest PMS and AGO depot prices together with key industry\n                developments and market news.\n            </p>\n\n            <br>\n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            PMS Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average PMS Prices: ₦1,183.50/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>LIQUID BULK</td>\n                <td>₦1,190.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>BULK STRATEGIC</td>\n                <td>₦1,190.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SIGMUND</td>\n                <td>₦1,190.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MASTERS</td>\n                <td>₦1,190.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>PARKER</td>\n                <td>₦1,182.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>NIPCO LAGOS</td>\n                <td>₦1,166.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AITEO</td>\n                <td>₦1,165.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MATRIX PH</td>\n                <td>₦1,195.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            AGO Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average AGO Prices: ₦1,618.75/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>NIPCO LAGOS</td>\n                <td>₦1,650.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>INTERGRATED</td>\n                <td>₦1,600.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,600.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DUPORT</td>\n                <td>₦1,600.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBETO</td>\n                <td>₦1,700.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SAHARA</td>\n                <td>₦1,600.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MENJ</td>\n                <td>₦1,600.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>A.A RANO</td>\n                <td>₦1,600.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Strait of Hormuz Traffic Worsens as Brent Crude Nears $90\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude was trading at $88.04 per barrel, up 0.36%. West Texas Intermediate (WTI) stood at $82.50, gaining 0.45 per cent. Murban crude was quoted at $84.90, up 5.79 per cent, while natural gas declined 0.64 per cent to $2.776.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/strait-of-hormuz-traffic-worsens-as-brent-crude-nears-90\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Depot Diesel Prices Jump as Marketers Anticipate Crude Oil Surge Amid Hormuz Uncertainty\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria’s diesel market turned sharply bullish on Monday as depot owners raised Automotive Gas Oil (AGO) prices. The sharp intra-day adjustments came as marketers reassessed the market following the rise in crude oil prices. A number of depots reportedly stopped selling during the day rather than commit available volumes at their earlier prices.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/depot-diesel-prices-jump-as-marketers-anticipate-crude-oil-surge-amid-hormuz-uncertainty\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Surge 4% as Strait of Hormuz Reopening Hopes Fade\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude was trading at $86.68 per barrel, up 3.75 percent. West Texas Intermediate (WTI) stood at $81.12, gaining 3.76 percent. The renewed rally followed Iran's demand that the United States meet several conditions before restrictions are lifted.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-surge-4-as-strait-of-hormuz-reopening-hopes-fade\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Fuel Subsidy Could Have Cost Nigeria ₦53tn Without Reform — NRS Chair\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria’s fuel subsidy bill could have climbed to approximately ₦53 trillion, while the naira could have weakened to ⁦3,500 per dollar, if the subsidy regime had remained in place. Chairman of the Nigeria Revenue Service, Zacch Adedeji, made the projection while defending President Bola Tinubu's economic reforms.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/fuel-subsidy-could-have-cost-nigeria-53tn-without-reform-nrs-chair\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    UK Buys £674.5m Nigerian Refined Fuel, Overtaking Crude Oil\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Refined petroleum products have emerged as the United Kingdom’s largest goods import from Nigeria, accounting for 47.5 per cent of total Nigerian goods imported by Britain. The shift marks a notable change in the composition of Nigeria's exports to the UK, where crude oil has traditionally held the largest share. The change was driven partly by a sharp reduction in British purchases of Nigerian crude.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/uk-buys-6745m-nigerian-refined-fuel-overtaking-crude-oil\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
